From 0e0df1e1a6335180f123dcc331d7f8e1d2156e08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 16:27:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] bugfix: Keep active-goal parents available while children run

Red: just test -p codex-app-server -E test(app_server_resumes_parent_after_background_child_finishes) starts an unsolicited active-goal parent turn before child completion; the ordinary control passes.
Green: both public JSON-RPC parent scenarios pass. The goal remains Active during waiting, the parent answers an unrelated prompt while the child runs, and completion resumes the parent to complete its goal. Existing no-child goal continuation also passes.

Scope: live-process best-effort delivery; no restart replay, task UI, or Monitor support.
